      "id": "F02",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`topic-02.mdx`, The rhetorical triangle and Issue questions and information questions; assessment RRQ 4 model: “Request plus an offer” to Rubina is declared to argue nothing, even though a reciprocal duty offer can be a reason for accepting the request. “Arguments belong to issue questions” excludes reasoned factual conclusions even though Topic 2.2 itself offers a causal vacancy argument. Administrative power to grant leave does not determine whether a text supplies support. Teach communicative purpose and support relations with contextual qualification; allow colleagues and parents to receive arguments.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F03",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`topic-03.mdx`, Classify first, judge second; `sources/texts/yuzenker2022.md`, Scope note: Candidate attributes a specific methodological position and “cart before the horse” wording to Yu and Zenker. The bound source explicitly calls the position a title-level inference, says full text was not retrieved, and supplies no supporting quoted passage. This is an evidence mismatch, not proof the published authors never said it. Bind the actual supporting passage and locator or remove the unverified attribution. Do not treat a source note's inference as a verified quotation.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F04",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`topic-01.mdx` through `topic-04.mdx`, Further reading; `topic-03.mdx`, opening of Types of argument; `sources/unit-02.md`, Unverifiable sources: Bassham is declared bibliographic-only, but prose says its chapters “supply” the distinctions, “source for ... argument types and their characteristic weaknesses”, and attributes recurring types to it without point-of-use disclosure. D-2026-0013 explicitly requires the bibliographic limitation at the point of use. The source declaration also lacks a dated retrieval-attempt record. Restore honest point-of-use limits and bind verifiable support for specific taxonomies. Qin's bound abstract supports the qualified sixteen-student instructional finding, not a universal argument taxonomy. Malone's bound file is a scope summary, not source passages sufficient to check every attributed recommendation.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F05",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`unit-assessment.mdx`, RRQ 7 and corresponding model: Prompt states only that three of four adopting schools improved. It gives neither an explicit causal conclusion nor a comparison with non-adopters. Model awards two marks for closing a gap to a causal conclusion and mentions schools that did not add classes, which the question never supplies. State the intended conclusion/comparison or accept the report-only reading and conditional reconstruction.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F06",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`unit-assessment.mdx`, RRQ 9 and model; `topic-04.mdx`, worked letter and formative item 6: “Hira has missed eleven days” plus “route should be restored” needs a causal/feasibility bridge as well as an attendance duty. The model supplies only duty and asserts that refusal rejects that duty. A head may accept the duty and dispute route causation or available remedies. Accept multiple defensible assumptions and distinguish missing empirical links from normative obligations.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F07",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`unit-assessment.mdx`, ERQ 3 and rubric: Four teachers are not four distinct taught types: notebook and pass-rate reasons are both evidence-shaped, followed by analogy and feasibility/policy. Topic 2.3 expressly says nobody in that meeting used authority. Rubric “all four types correctly named” risks requiring authority where none is present. Credit mixed/repeated patterns or supply four genuinely distinct cases; require evidence-based rankings without a single predetermined order.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F08",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`static/img/figures/efmp-304/unit-02/fig-U2-2.svg` and `.dark.svg`; `fig-U2-4.svg` and `.dark.svg`: Geometry measures U2-2 inference-label overflow of 21.7 and 43.1px beyond its 780px viewBox. Native screenshot visibly cuts off both lines. U2-4's last column heading runs into the preceding heading and extends 1.7px beyond the 900px viewBox; screenshot confirms collision. Separate author must reflow labels and regenerate dark variants. `check:figures` passes despite these defects.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F09",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "message": "`unit-assessment.mdx`, RRQ 8, RRQ 10, ERQ 5 and rubrics: RRQ 8 mostly recalls cue words with an explanation, despite Apply. RRQ 10 classifies near-identical taught examples, despite Analyze. ERQ 5 requests analysis and evaluative judgement, and its own rubric explicitly says Evaluate despite a Create label. Judge tags from actual work and align them; no new Create requirement is inferred from the blueprint's optional Evaluate/Create range.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F10",
      "severity": "uncertain",
      "message": "Required independent handoff and `render-review`: Missing actual author-run identity, parent-frozen handoff, and exact deployed model revision prevent full provenance verification. No fresh Docusaurus rendering supplied; brief forbids a build/server. Native SVG screenshots are supplementary and do not satisfy 360px layout, keyboard table access, or A4 print review. Owner/host must supply provenance and a permitted rendering handoff; obtain a fresh review after repairs.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F11",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "message": "Bound `course-overview.mdx`, Assessment: Course overview claims default 60/40, but guide lines 743-756 and this unit/spec use course-specific 30/70. Guide settles the answer. This dependency is outside the unit-edit scope, so refer repair to the course owner; this reviewer did not change it.",
      "resolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F12",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "message": "`unit-assessment.mdx`, MCQ 3; `topic-01.mdx`, dispute test: MCQ 3 assumes without context that nobody disputes the fan failure. B matches the intended explanatory reading, but causal wording can also supply evidence for a disputed fact. Add the audience context and keep “dispute” a heuristic rather than an exhaustive definition.",
      "resolved": false
    }
